    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n9243" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Cōmē</span></b> ,
		ēs, f., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Κώμη</span> (a village). <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			Come Hiera, <i>a town in Caria</i>, <i>with a temple and an oracle of Apollo</i>, <i><span class="en">Liv. 38,
				12, 9</span></i>. —</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> Xylina Come, <i>a small town in
			Pisidia</i>, Liv 38, 15, 7.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>III.</b> Acoridos Come, <i>a small town in
				Phrygia</i>, Liv 38, 15, 12 Weissenb. ad loc.</div>
